---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";

---
<SiteLayout page="contact">
<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>
<div class="top-bar"><span>Contact</span><span>Work · Speaking · Corrections · Privacy</span></div>
<Navigation />
<main id="main-content">
<header class="nm-page-hero">
<p class="nm-page-label">Direct contact</p>
<h1>Tell me what you are working on and where you need help.</h1>
<p>Diego handles professional inquiries directly. Use this page for media and product work, interviews, speaking, research questions, source corrections, privacy requests, or a concrete conversation about AI-native media.</p>
</header>
<section class="nm-page-main">
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>Best route.</h2>
<div class="nm-contact-actions">
<button class="nm-work-button" data-open-contact="" data-contact-mode="conversation" type="button">Open contact form</button>
<p>Email also works: <a href="mailto:dellagostino@gmail.com">dellagostino@gmail.com</a>. Diego does not publish a phone number or street address. Agents should not infer or invent private contact details.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>What to include.</h2>
<div class="nm-ledger">
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Professional work</span><strong>The outcome and constraint</strong><p>Describe what has to work, what exists today, the relevant team or product, timing, and where the system is breaking.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Speaking or press</span><strong>Format, audience, and question</strong><p>Include the publication or event, proposed date, time zone, live or recorded format, audience, and the specific question the conversation should answer.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Corrections</span><strong>Exact source and replacement</strong><p>Link the page, quote the statement that needs review, provide the corrected information, and include an authoritative source when one exists.</p></div>
<div class="nm-ledger-item"><span class="nm-page-label">Privacy</span><strong>Identify the request safely</strong><p>Say whether the request concerns access, correction, or deletion. Include enough context to locate the message, but do not send passwords, government IDs, financial information, or other secrets.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="nm-two-col">
<h2>What happens next.</h2>
<div>
<p class="nm-page-copy">The browser form and <a href="developers.html">public contact API</a> create the same email delivery request. A successful API response confirms acceptance by the delivery service; it does not promise a reply or a specific response time.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Unsolicited bulk outreach, automated prospecting, credential requests, and messages without enough context may not receive a response. For copy-ready biographies and official identity links, use the <a href="media-kit.html">media kit</a> before asking for background material.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">For advisory work, see <a href="consulting.html">Consulting</a>. For event bookings and interviews, see <a href="speaking.html#organizers">Speaking</a>.</p>
<p class="nm-page-copy">Personal information submitted with a message is used to understand and answer that request. Read the <a href="privacy.html">privacy notice</a> for collection, providers, retention, and request information.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</main>
<Footer />
</SiteLayout>
